WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.796
ADDIE is a practical instructional design framework for moving from a learning need to a finished learning experience.

2
00:00:07.796 --> 00:00:12.504
The name stands for Analyze, Design, Develop, Implement, and Evaluate.

3
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:24.700
Those five words describe the major decisions course creators make: understand the problem, plan the experience, build the materials, deliver the course, and use evidence to improve it.

4
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:35.969
For eLearning, ADDIE is useful because it keeps the team from jumping straight into screens, tools, graphics, or narration before the instructional problem is understood.

5
00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.671
Many weak courses begin as content dumps.

6
00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:47.084
A policy document, slide deck, or manual is copied into a course shell, a quiz is added at the end, and the result is called training.

7
00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:54.417
ADDIE pushes the team to ask what learners need to do differently, not only what information they need to receive.

8
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:59.820
ADDIE should be treated as a flexible workflow, not a rigid waterfall requirement.

9
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:12.942
In real projects, analysis can reveal design constraints, design can expose content gaps, development can uncover technical issues, and evaluation can send the team back to revise earlier decisions.

10
00:01:12.942 --> 00:01:15.257
The value of ADDIE is not paperwork.

11
00:01:15.257 --> 00:01:18.885
The value is disciplined thinking at the right moments.

12
00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:22.745
It also helps separate related but different kinds of work.

13
00:01:22.745 --> 00:01:28.070
Instructional design defines objectives, strategy, practice, and assessment.

14
00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:32.393
Media production creates graphics, audio, video, and documents.

15
00:01:32.393 --> 00:01:35.944
Course authoring assembles the learning experience.

16
00:01:35.944 --> 00:01:39.031
LMS publishing handles delivery and tracking.

17
00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:41.733
Evaluation measures quality and impact.

18
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:46.673
When those roles are clear, the course becomes easier to build and maintain.

19
00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:50.069
The practical purpose of ADDIE is decision support.

20
00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:59.871
It helps teams avoid tool-first development, vague objectives, decorative interactions, and assessments that do not measure the intended outcome.

21
00:01:59.871 --> 00:02:07.359
A structured process creates room for creativity because the team knows what problem the course is trying to solve.
